      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] ❌ **Changes Requested — Please split this CL**\n\n### Review Summary\n\n**CL Size \u0026 Scope:**\n*   This CL is reported as `Size: L (+761, -0)`. Per `go/small-cls`, CLs of this size are too large to review effectively as a single atomic unit and must be split. The previous review requested a split, which was marked as \"Done\", but the CL remains a single monolithic commit.\n*   **Proposed Split Plan:**\n    *   **CL 1:** Add the base `RtsUsbDevice` class structure and USB initialization/detachment/cleanup logic.\n    *   **CL 2:** Implement the core DFU download protocol and polling logic within `RtsUsbDevice`.\n    *   **CL 3:** Add the command-line utility entry point (`main`, `parse_args`, `read_file`) and build system integration.\n\n**Testing \u0026 Test Coverage:**\n*   **Missing Tests:** Despite previous feedback, there are still no automated unit tests for the pure logic components (such as `parse_args` and `read_file`). When splitting this CL, please add a small suite of unit tests for these pure helpers.\n\n**Functionality \u0026 Robustness:**\n*   **Resource Leaks (Rule of Three):** `RtsUsbDevice` lacks deleted copy/assignment operators, making it vulnerable to double-frees of the libusb context if copied. See inline comment.\n\n**Idiomaticity \u0026 Readability:**\n*   A few remaining magic numbers (`1000`, `10000`, `60000`) should be extracted into `constexpr` constants.\n\n**Commit Message:**\n*   The first line should end with a period.\n*   The `TEST\u003d` footer still just lists the command run rather than the outcome.\n\nPlease split the CL into a stacked series and address the inline comments.\n[🔗](http://go/tj/5213bd81-d1c0-4dda-ae7d-88393b98a74e)",
