      "side": 1,
      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] **Resource Encapsulation \u0026 The Rule of Three:** `RtsUsbDevice` manually manages `libusb` resources (`ctx_`, `dev_handle_`) and frees them in its destructor. However, it implicitly allows copying, which would lead to a double-free of the libusb context if a copy is destroyed.\n\nPlease explicitly delete the copy constructor and copy assignment operator to ensure move-only or single-ownership semantics:\n```cpp\n\tRtsUsbDevice(const RtsUsbDevice\u0026) \u003d delete;\n\tRtsUsbDevice\u0026 operator\u003d(const RtsUsbDevice\u0026) \u003d delete;\n```\n[🔗](http://go/tj/5213bd81-d1c0-4dda-ae7d-88393b98a74e)",
